# A document index whose rebase was never finished

This is the shape that reached a commit at `889763e` and that nothing in the
repository noticed. The extension is `.md.fixture` rather than `.md` on purpose:
the check refuses `.md`, and a fixture that the check would refuse cannot itself
be committed as one.

| 047 | a row that survived the rebase |
<<<<<<< HEAD
| 048 | main's version of the row |
||||||| parent of abc1234 (a commit message)
| 048 | the common ancestor's version |
=======
| 048 | this branch's version of the row |
>>>>>>> abc1234 (a commit message)
| 050 | another row that survived |

Below are the shapes that are NOT markers and must never be flagged, because a
check whose false positives are routine is a check people learn to bypass:

=====

---

> a blockquote
>>> a nested blockquote, which is three characters and not seven
